@prefix ldh:    <https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix dh:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<> a dh:Item ;
    dct:title "Upload file" ;
    dct:description "Learn how to upload files to LinkedDataHub" ;
    rdf:_1 <#content> .
    
<#content> a ldh:XHTML ;
    rdf:value """<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <p class="lead">Learn how to upload files to LinkedDataHub</p>
    <div class="tabbable">
        <ul class="nav nav-tabs">
            <li class="active"><a>User interface</a></li>
            <li><a>Command line interface</a></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tab-content">
            <div class="tab-pane active">
                <div>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Click the <span class="btn btn-primary create-action">Create <span class="caret"></span></span> dropdown on the bottom of the page</li>
                        <li>Click on <samp>File</samp> in the drop-down list that appears</li>
                        <li>Fill out the mandatory <dfn>File</dfn> fields in the form:
                            <dl>
                                <dt>FileName</dt>
                                <dd>Select file from your filesystem</dd>
                                <dt>Title</dt>
                                <dd>Enter file title</dd>
                            </dl>
                        </li>
                        <li>Click <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span></li>
                    </ol>
                    <p>See how below:</p>
                    <div class="screenshot-placeholder">
                        <span class="msi" aria-hidden="true">play_circle</span>
                        <p>Screen recording: uploading a file</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="tab-pane">
                <div>
                    <p>A file is uploaded to the document that will hold it, so create that document first. Uploading Nancy Davolio's portrait from the Northwind demo:</p>
                    <pre>doc=$(ldh create-item \\
  --title "Nancy Davolio" \\
  --container "${LDH_BASE}employees/")

ldh add-file \\
  --title "nancy.jpg" \\
  --file employees/nancy.jpg \\
  --content-type image/jpeg \\
  "$doc"</pre>
                    <p>The command prints the content-addressed URI of the upload as its only output:</p>
                    <pre>https://localhost:4443/uploads/fb2e87988887cebf252947ba5d98e34d01d44ed4</pre>
                    <p>That URI is stable across instances — it is derived from the file content alone — which is what lets the
                        <a href="../../tutorial/media/" target="_blank">Northwind CSVs</a> reference their images by hash before they are even uploaded.
                        <code>--content-type</code> is optional — the media type is detected from the file when it is not given.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="alert alert-warning">
        <h4>Note about ontology files</h4>
        <p>If you upload an ontology file (RDF/OWL), be aware that it will not be automatically loaded via <code>owl:imports</code> declarations.
        This is a technical limitation to prevent circular dependencies during system initialization.</p>
        <p>For more information on working with ontologies, see the <a href="../../reference/administration/ontologies/">ontologies reference documentation</a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>"""^^rdf:XMLLiteral .